1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,510
A NASA telescope just fell out of the sky.
一台 NASA 望远镜刚刚从天上掉下来，

2
00:00:02,510 --> 00:00:05,100
It burned up over Indonesia on November fourth.
十一月四日在印度尼西亚上空烧掉了。

3
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:06,130
Its name was Swift.
它叫 Swift（雨燕），

4
00:00:06,130 --> 00:00:08,970
It weighed about fourteen hundred and fifty kilos.
重约一千四百五十公斤。

5
00:00:08,970 --> 00:00:09,840
What killed it?
是什么杀死了它？

6
00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:11,570
Air. Almost nothing but air.
空气。几乎什么都没有的空气。

7
00:00:11,570 --> 00:00:12,650
Today's brain teaser:
今天的烧脑问题：

8
00:00:12,650 --> 00:00:15,340
how does nearly empty space pull down a telescope?
几乎空荡荡的太空，怎么能把望远镜拽下来？

9
00:00:15,340 --> 00:00:17,510
Meet Swift: launched in two thousand four,
认识 Swift：2004 年发射，

10
00:00:17,510 --> 00:00:19,280
about six hundred kilometers up.
在大约六百公里高的地方。

11
00:00:19,280 --> 00:00:20,980
Its job: catch gamma ray bursts,
它的任务：抓伽马射线暴，

12
00:00:20,980 --> 00:00:23,170
the biggest explosions in the universe.
宇宙里最猛烈的爆炸。

13
00:00:23,170 --> 00:00:24,670
It could swing around and point
它能在大约一分钟里转身对准目标，

14
00:00:24,670 --> 00:00:26,440
in about a minute. Hence the name.
所以叫“雨燕”。

15
00:00:26,440 --> 00:00:27,660
Planned life: two years.
原计划只工作两年，

16
00:00:27,660 --> 00:00:29,410
It worked for almost twenty two.
结果干了将近二十二年。

17
00:00:29,410 --> 00:00:31,800
It caught more than a thousand of those bursts.
它抓到了一千多次伽马暴，

18
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:33,350
Not bad for a two year plan.
对一个两年的计划来说，相当不错。

19
00:00:33,350 --> 00:00:34,190
Now the physics.
现在讲物理：在轨道上，

20
00:00:34,190 --> 00:00:36,420
In orbit, Swift is falling all the time.
Swift 其实一直在往下掉。

21
00:00:36,420 --> 00:00:37,900
It just moves sideways so fast
只是它横着飞得太快，

22
00:00:37,900 --> 00:00:39,640
that it keeps missing the ground.
总是掉不到地面上。

23
00:00:39,640 --> 00:00:41,950
About seven point six kilometers per second.
每秒大约七点六公里，

24
00:00:41,950 --> 00:00:44,420
Around the whole world in ninety six minutes.
九十六分钟绕地球一圈。

25
00:00:44,420 --> 00:00:46,590
But up there, there's still a tiny bit of air.
可那么高的地方，还有一丁点空气，

26
00:00:46,590 --> 00:00:48,080
Like a whisper of a headwind.
就像一阵极轻的逆风。

27
00:00:48,080 --> 00:00:49,760
Every orbit, that whisper steals
每绕一圈，这阵逆风

28
00:00:49,760 --> 00:00:50,980
a tiny bit of energy.
就偷走它一点点能量。

29
00:00:50,980 --> 00:00:52,810
Lose energy, drop a little lower.
能量少了，就降低一点；

30
00:00:52,810 --> 00:00:55,150
Lower air is thicker, so it steals more.
越低空气越浓，偷得越多。

31
00:00:55,150 --> 00:00:56,080
It's a snowball.
像滚雪球：

32
00:00:56,080 --> 00:00:57,940
Slow at first, then very fast.
一开始很慢，后来非常快。

33
00:00:57,940 --> 00:00:59,290
Twist one: as it drops,
反转一：往下掉的时候，

34
00:00:59,290 --> 00:01:00,880
Swift actually speeds up.
Swift 反而越飞越快。

35
00:01:00,880 --> 00:01:02,730
A lower orbit is a faster orbit.
轨道越低，绕得越快。

36
00:01:02,730 --> 00:01:05,670
Drag makes satellites go faster. Weird, but true.
空气阻力让卫星加速，怪，但是真的。

37
00:01:05,670 --> 00:01:06,650
Twist two: the Sun
反转二：是太阳

38
00:01:06,650 --> 00:01:07,910
made the air thicker.
把空气变浓了。

39
00:01:07,910 --> 00:01:10,760
When the Sun is very active, it heats the upper air,
太阳活跃时，会把高层大气加热，

40
00:01:10,760 --> 00:01:13,060
and the air puffs up, like bread rising.
空气就像面包发酵一样鼓起来。

41
00:01:13,060 --> 00:01:15,200
Suddenly there's more air at Swift's height.
于是 Swift 那个高度，突然多了空气。

42
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:16,290
More air, more drag.
空气越多，阻力越大。

43
00:01:16,290 --> 00:01:19,550
The Sun has been in a busy stretch of its eleven year cycle.
太阳正处在十一年周期里很忙的一段。

44
00:01:19,550 --> 00:01:21,630
NASA says that made the decay worse.
NASA 说，这让下降更快了。

45
00:01:21,630 --> 00:01:22,510
By late October,
到十月下旬，

46
00:01:22,510 --> 00:01:25,910
Swift was down to about two hundred seventy five kilometers.
Swift 只剩大约二百七十五公里高。

47
00:01:25,910 --> 00:01:27,690
So NASA tried something new:
于是 NASA 试了个新办法：

48
00:01:27,690 --> 00:01:28,760
a robot rescue.
派机器人去救它。

49
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:32,030
A company called Catalyst built a robot spacecraft named Link,
一家叫 Katalyst 的公司造了救援飞船 LINK，

50
00:01:32,030 --> 00:01:33,890
to grab Swift and push it higher.
要抓住 Swift，把它推高。

51
00:01:33,890 --> 00:01:34,950
It launched in July,
它七月发射，

52
00:01:34,950 --> 00:01:37,040
on a rocket dropped from an airplane.
用的是从飞机上扔下去的火箭。

53
00:01:37,040 --> 00:01:39,060
But the rescue did not work out in time.
可救援没能及时成功，

54
00:01:39,060 --> 00:01:41,640
The exact reasons haven't been made fully public.
具体原因还没有完全公开。

55
00:01:41,640 --> 00:01:42,840
Twist three: the fireball
反转三：那团火球，

56
00:01:42,840 --> 00:01:44,310
does not come from friction.
不是摩擦出来的。

57
00:01:44,310 --> 00:01:47,750
Swift hit thick air at about twenty seven thousand kilometers an hour.
Swift 以每小时两万七千公里冲进浓空气，

58
00:01:47,750 --> 00:01:50,080
The air in front couldn't get out of the way.
前面的空气根本来不及让开。

59
00:01:50,080 --> 00:01:51,620
Squeezed air gets super hot,
空气被猛压，就变得超级烫，

60
00:01:51,620 --> 00:01:54,590
like a bike pump getting warm, but far more extreme.
像打气筒会发热，只是猛烈得多。

61
00:01:54,590 --> 00:01:55,800
That squeezed air glows,
被压缩的空气发光，

62
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:58,050
and the spacecraft melts and breaks apart.
飞船熔化、解体。

63
00:01:58,050 --> 00:01:59,330
Most of Swift burned up.
Swift 大部分都烧掉了。

64
00:01:59,330 --> 00:02:03,550
NASA put the risk to anyone on the ground at about one in twenty one hundred.
NASA 估计，伤到地面任何人的概率约二千一百分之一。

65
00:02:03,550 --> 00:02:05,200
Fine print: why the rescue failed
友情提示：救援为什么失败，

66
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:07,230
is still mostly unexplained in public.
目前公开的信息还不多。

67
00:02:07,230 --> 00:02:08,890
And drag changes with the Sun,
而且阻力跟着太阳变，

68
00:02:08,890 --> 00:02:12,040
so reentry times always come with hours of uncertainty.
所以坠落时间总有十几个小时的误差。

69
00:02:12,040 --> 00:02:14,630
So how does almost nothing pull down a telescope?
几乎没有的空气，怎么拽下望远镜？

70
00:02:14,630 --> 00:02:17,220
A tiny push, every orbit, for twenty two years.
每圈推一下，推了二十二年。

71
00:02:17,220 --> 00:02:18,580
Swift was named for speed.
Swift 因速度得名，

72
00:02:18,580 --> 00:02:20,820
In the end, speed is what burned it.
最后也是速度把它烧掉了。

